# Р146, the variant without an own value (entry Main): the root's x has no value. Main's input x is filled by
# `x := 9`; C's input x has no actual and no value of its own, so it is filled from the same-named place of the
# immediate caller, Main's 9 (#binding-autofill). seen 9.
# Red until autofill takes the current value of a loaded source place: Main's x is declared without a value and
# written later, and the kernel gives C's x no value, so the read answers 5 (#binding-autofill).
int: seen 0
int: x
C:
    node\seen := x
Main:
    x := 9
    C()
